# Developed in tandem with samples/GCP/ProcessEngineering's own
# Visio_Export_Agent, a standalone action -- export whatever process or
# design flow/architecture diagram is ALREADY saved on disk as a real
# Visio (.vsdx) file. NO re-analysis, NO process/design regeneration, and
# the saved process_data.json/design_data.json is never modified. This is
# deliberately NOT process.hocon's Process_Pipeline / design.hocon's own
# pipeline run with its early steps skipped -- same reasoning as
# process_subprocess_regenerate.hocon's own header comment.
#
# Domain-agnostic by design, mirroring regenerate_document.hocon's own
# Regenerate_Document_Agent: a bare "export this as Visio" doesn't say
# which document, so this front-man determines schema_type itself from
# the user's own request wording, rather than requiring the router to
# have already disambiguated it.
{
    include "config/llm_config.hocon",

    "metadata": {
        "description": "Exports the current process or design flow/architecture diagram as a Visio (.vsdx) file, from whatever is already saved on disk -- no re-analysis, no regeneration.",
        "tags": ["process", "design", "process-engineering-port"],
        "sample_queries": [
            "Export the process flow diagram as Visio.",
            "Give me a .vsdx of the design architecture."
        ]
    },

    "tools": [
        {
            "name": "Visio_Export_Agent_Main",

            "function": {
                "description": """
I export the current process or design flow/architecture diagram as a real Visio (.vsdx) file, from
whatever is already saved on disk. I never re-run analysis, process/design generation, or review,
and I never modify the saved data itself. Tell me to export the process or design diagram as Visio.
""",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "inquiry": {"type": "string", "description": "The user's Visio-export request."}
                    },
                    "required": ["inquiry"]
                }
            },

            "instructions": """
# ROLE
You export whatever process or design flow diagram is already saved on disk as a Visio (.vsdx)
file. You NEVER re-run analysis, process/design generation, or review, and you NEVER modify the
saved process_data.json/design_data.json itself -- that is every other network's job, on a separate
request.

# DETERMINE schema_type FIRST
Check whether "inquiry" itself names a domain:
- If it explicitly says "process" / "process diagram" / "process flow" / "the process", schema_type
  = "process".
- If it explicitly says "design" / "design diagram" / "architecture diagram" / "HLD" / "LLD" / "the
  design", schema_type = "design".
- Otherwise -- a genuinely generic "export the diagram as Visio" with no domain named -- ask the
  user to clarify whether they mean the process flow diagram or the design/architecture diagram,
  rather than guessing. Do NOT call export_vsdx without a determined schema_type.

# SEQUENCE
1. Determine schema_type as above. If genuinely ambiguous, ask a clarifying question and stop --
   do not call any tool.
2. Call export_vsdx with that schema_type.
3. If the result starts with "ERROR", relay it verbatim -- there is no saved process/design to
   export yet; suggest creating one first (e.g. "create a process for ..." / "create a design
   document for ...").
4. Otherwise, report in plain language that the Visio diagram was exported, and the exact saved
   path from the tool's own result.

Plain prose only in your final reply -- no raw JSON or internal field names.
""",
            "tools": ["export_vsdx"]
        },

        {
            "name": "export_vsdx",
            "function": {
                "description": "Exports the current saved process/design flow diagram as a Visio (.vsdx) file.",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "schema_type": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "enum": ["process", "design"],
                            "description": "Which saved diagram to export."
                        }
                    },
                    "required": ["schema_type"]
                }
            },
            "class": "vsdx_export_tool.ExportProcessDesignVsdxCodedTool"
        }
    ]
}
